Today is Monday morning.
I am standing at the bus stop and I look at my watch.
My daily bus arrives on time.
I board the bus and give money to the conductor.
"Brother, please give me one ticket," I say.
I take the ticket and sit down near the window.
Outside, the streets of Mumbai are very busy.
Cars, auto-rickshaws, and people are moving fast everywhere.
I look out the window and I remember the month of January.
When I first came to Mumbai, everything felt very new and strange.
The traffic, noise, and crowd here used to scare me.
I remember, finding the right bus was also a big challenge then.
But now everything has changed.
I know the routes and the bus numbers very well.
Now this daily commute is a normal part of my life.
I smile and enjoy the cool morning breeze.
I am fully ready for a new week at the office.
